sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor H as Release team
    participant P as Release pipeline
    participant G as Shared Git repository
    box Selected OpenShift site
        participant C as Argo CD
        participant R as Argo Rollouts
        participant S as Service Mesh
        participant M as Monitoring
    end

    Note over H,M: SUCCESS - both sites start on v1. CI has built and tested v2
    Note over C,M: Each site has its own Argo CD, Rollouts, mesh and monitoring

    loop Release DC-A first, then DC-B only after A is fully promoted and healthy
        H->>P: Approve release for the selected site
        P->>G: Open PR changing only that site's version to v2
        H->>G: Review and merge the release PR
        C->>G: Fetch approved site configuration
        G-->>C: Desired application version is v2
        C->>R: Sync the site's Rollout configuration
        R->>R: Start v2 canary while keeping stable v1 available

        loop Local canary traffic - 10%, then 50% after checks pass
            R->>S: Update the site's canary traffic policy
            S->>S: Split local Orders requests between v1 and v2
            R->>R: Allow warm-up before analysis
            R->>M: Request canary health measurements
            M-->>R: Return measured service health
            R->>R: Evaluate and pass the configured health checks
        end

        R->>R: Pause for final promotion approval
        H->>M: Review fresh telemetry and end-to-end checks
        M-->>H: Return current health evidence
        H->>R: Approve promotion for this site
        R->>R: Promote v2 to the stable release
        R->>S: Direct 100% of local Orders traffic to stable v2
        H->>H: Verify full promotion and full-traffic health before accepting the site
    end

    Note over C,M: Both sites now serve v2. Each site's rollout was independent
    Note over G,S: GTM site distribution stays unchanged. Canary percentages apply within the selected site

